 [17592186049939 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049939 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049939 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049939 #edb/ref 1031 "Distributing the Negative Sign in a Linear Expression" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049939 #edb/ref 1033 137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049939 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "20058901-3844-51ce-a107-70205a1553fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1031 "Solving Two-Variable Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1033 356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050622 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "59bac138-6475-51d1-971d-3bd216b92f3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1031 "Applying the Distributive Law With Linear Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1033 135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050908 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "704c70d6-1bf4-5b23-b4da-d122a744acda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110320 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13077" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110320 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{2x+5}{30} = \\dfrac{1}{2}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110320 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7df7a073-8131-5732-b353-f89484052e38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110320 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2x + 5}{30} &= \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n(2x + 5) \\cdot 2 &= 30 \\cdot 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(2x + 5) \\cdot 2 &= 30 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n4x + 10 &= 30 \\\\\n4x + 10 - 10 &= 30 - 10 \\\\\n4x &= 20 \\\\\n\\frac{4x}{4} &= \\frac{20}{4} \\\\\nx &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110321 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13078" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110321 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $x$, where $\\dfrac{6-2x}{2} = \\dfrac{6-x}{3}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110321 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4041cf6f-61b8-5794-9988-436722985bcd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110321 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{6 - 2x}{2} &= \\frac{6 - x}{3} \\\\\n(6 - 2x) \\cdot 3 &= 2 \\cdot (6 - x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(6 - 2x) \\cdot 3 &= 2 \\cdot (6 - x) \\\\\n18 - 6x &= 12 - 2x \\\\\n18 - 6x - 18 &= 12 - 2x - 18 \\\\\n- 6x &= -2x - 6 \\\\\n- 6x + 2x &= -2x - 6 + 2x \\\\\n- 4x &= -6 \\\\\n\\frac{-4x}{-4} &= \\frac{-6}{-4} \\\\\nx &= \\frac{6}{4} \\\\\nx &= \\frac{3}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110322 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13079" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110322 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $u$, where $\\dfrac{u+2}{3} =-\\dfrac{3-u}{2}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110322 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d97adcd5-65ea-5cf7-905a-db954e43904b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110322 #edb/ref 1074 "We transfer the negative into the numerator of the fraction, and proceed with cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{u + 2}{3} &= -\\frac{3 - u}{2} \\\\\n\\frac{u + 2}{3} &= (- (3 - u))/(2) \\\\\n\\frac{u + 2}{3} &= \\frac{-3 + u}{2} \\\\\n(u + 2) \\cdot 2 &= 3 \\cdot (-3 + u)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(u + 2) \\cdot 2 &= 3 \\cdot (-3 + u) \\\\\n2u + 4 &= -9 + 3u \\\\\n2u + 4 - 2u &= -9 + 3u - 2u \\\\\n4 &= -9 + u \\\\\n4 + 9 &= -9 + u + 9 \\\\\n13 &= u\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=13$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110619 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110619 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110619 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110619 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110619 #edb/ref 1039 "Cross-Multiplying with One Binomial" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110619 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110619 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "3ff2f965-b406-5c9a-bd41-73ccdce951eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110620 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110620 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110620 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110620 #edb/ref 1039 "Cross-Multiplying with Two Binomials" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110620 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110620 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e880edeb-82ad-5943-a846-dc3246e3e3bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110621 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110621 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110621 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110621 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186111121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110621 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110621 #edb/ref 1039 "Cross-Multiplying with a Negative Sign" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110621 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110621 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "59230000-ef0e-56c0-ab06-17676d817d5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110809 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110809 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110809 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110809 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110809 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110809 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110809 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Linear Equations Using Cross-Multiplication" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110809 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186111526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110809 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110809 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "224e6883-ecf1-58d2-8217-7503c15c1910" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111526 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111526 #edb/ref 1061 175966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111526 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "62154097-0663-58a8-8dfe-b1f260a5583e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111526 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111527 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111527 #edb/ref 1061 175967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111527 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "79e64205-d43a-5719-a973-65d5eb873b04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111527 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111528 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111528 #edb/ref 1061 175971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111528 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "39ea7244-0ca1-52cc-9e51-81973115c977" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111528 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111529 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111529 #edb/ref 1061 175974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111529 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a5826411-42a0-5ce0-aa7f-6e0d021d40fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111529 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111530 #edb/ref 1061 175975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111530 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1f42768c-0adb-5fc8-8dd3-b63229bed312" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111530 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111911 #edb/ref 1064 "If we have rational expressions on both sides of an equation, say,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{red}x-1}}{{\\color{blue}2}} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}2x-1}}{{\\color{red}5}}\n$$\n\nthen we can eliminate the rational expressions by applying **cross-multiplication**:\n\n- we cross-multiply the left-hand side numerator $({\\color{red}x-1})$ with the right-hand side denominator $({\\color{red}5})$, and\n- we cross-multiply the left-hand side denominator $({\\color{blue}2})$ with the right-hand side numerator $({\\color{blue}2x-1})$.\n\nDoing this, we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n({\\color{red}x-1}) \\cdot ({\\color{red}5}) = ({\\color{blue}2}) \\cdot ({\\color{blue}2x - 1})\n$$\n\nAfter we've cross-multiplied, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 1) \\cdot 5 &= 2 \\cdot (2x - 1) \\\\\n5x - 5 &= 4x - 2 \\\\\n5x - 5 + 5 &= 4x - 2 + 5 \\\\\n5x &= 4x + 3 \\\\\n5x - 4x &= 4x + 3 - 4x \\\\\nx &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** Cross-multiplication might seem magical, but it is really just a shortcut for multiplying both sides of the equation by each denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x - 1}{2} &= \\frac{2x - 1}{5} \\\\\n2 \\cdot \\frac{x - 1}{2} &= 2 \\cdot \\frac{2x - 1}{5} \\\\\n2 \\cdot \\frac{x - 1}{2} &= 2 \\cdot \\frac{2x - 1}{5} \\\\\nx - 1 &= 2 \\cdot \\frac{2x - 1}{5} \\\\\n(x - 1) \\cdot 5 &= 2 \\cdot \\frac{2x - 1}{5} \\cdot 5 \\\\\n(x - 1) \\cdot 5 &= 2 \\cdot \\frac{2x - 1}{5} \\cdot 5 \\\\\n(x - 1) \\cdot (5) &= (2) \\cdot (2x - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111911 #edb/ref 1065 8174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111911 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "99ff1453-e12b-518f-94b1-9baf8ee914e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111911 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111912 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x+1}{2} = -\\dfrac{x}{3}\n$$\n\nEven though one of the fractions is negative, we can still use cross-multiplication. All we have to do is transfer the negative into the numerator of the fraction, and proceed with cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x + 1}{2} &= -\\frac{x}{3} \\\\\n\\frac{x + 1}{2} &= \\frac{-x}{3} \\\\\n(x + 1) \\cdot 3 &= 2 \\cdot (-x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x + 1) \\cdot 3 &= 2 \\cdot (-x) \\\\\n3x + 3 &= -2x \\\\\n3x + 3 - 3x &= -2x - 3x \\\\\n3 &= -5x \\\\\n\\frac{3}{-5} &= \\frac{-5x}{-5} \\\\\n- \\frac{3}{5} &= x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx = -\\dfrac{3}{5}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111912 #edb/ref 1065 8175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111912 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ed67f4e3-4ff1-5900-bda0-c7f4e2b5a652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111912 #edb/ref 1067 "Cross-Multiplying with a Negative Sign" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
